(537, NULL, ''6. Prepare the environment, ensure adequate lighting, ventilation, and privacy ? mark'', ''0, 0.25, 0.5'', NULL),
(538, NULL, ''7. Position the patient in a high Fowler?s or sitting position, with head flexed slightly forward to prevent entry into the trachea. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(539, NULL, ''8. Protect the patient?s clothing with a towel or a mackintosh. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(540, NULL, ''9. Inspect the nostrils for patency and select the more patent nostril for insertion. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(541, NULL, ''10. Measure the length of the tube to be inserted, from the tip of the nose to the ear lobe, then to the xiphoid process, and mark it with adhesive tape or a pen. 2 marks'', ''0, 1, 2'', NULL),
(542, NULL, ''12. Lubricate the distal 10?15 cm of the tube with water-soluble jelly to ease insertion. 1Mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(543, NULL, ''13. Gently insert the tube along the floor of the selected nostril, directing backward and downward. 1? mark'', ''0, 1, 1.5'', NULL),
(544, NULL, ''14. When the tube reaches the oropharynx, instruct the patient to swallow as the tube advances. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(545, NULL, ''15. Observe patient?s response; stop immediately if coughing, choking, or cyanosis occurs (may indicate tracheal entry). Withdraw tube slightly and reattempt if safe. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(546, NULL, ''16. Confirm placement: aspirate gastric contents and test with litmus paper (acidic pH) or inject air and auscultate over the epigastrium for gurgling sound. 1 ? mark'', ''0, 1, 1.5'', NULL),
(547, NULL, ''17. Alternatively, immerse the tube end in water; air bubbles indicate wrong placement in the airway. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(548, NULL, ''18. Once confirmed, close the distal end with a spigot and secure the tube on the nose/cheek with adhesive tape to prevent dislodgment. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(549, NULL, ''19. Make the patient comfortable, place in semi-Fowler?s position, and clean any lubricant or secretions. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(550, NULL, ''20. Dispose of used items safely in appropriate waste containers, remove gloves, wash hands, and tidy the bedside. 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(551, NULL, ''21. Document the procedure 1 mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
