(840, 65, ''Pick the fetal skull model, introduce it as a model  1/2mark'', ''0,0.25,0.5'', NULL),
(841, 65, ''Defines the fetal skull as a flexible structure that undergoes molding in order to passed the maternal pelvis during birth. 1/2marks'', ''0,0.25,0.5'', NULL),
(842, 65, ''Comprises of the vault, face and base.: Region of the fetal skull are 4.:  i)The vault or caldarium- is the top part and most significant in child bearing. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(843, 65, ''ii)The vertex- is at the area between the fontanelles 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(844, 65, ''iii) face- starts from the orbit/ridge to the chin 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(845, 65, ''iv)The base- is a firmly ossified structure that covers and protect the brain stem 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(846, 65, ''Key features of the fetal skull are bones, sutures and fontanelles, which are membranous space. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(847, 65, ''Anatomical features are:   Bones- 2 frontal, 2parietal 2temporal and one occiput bones. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(848, 65, ''Sutures ?are fibrous joints that separates the bones. They are sagittal, coronal, lambdoid and frontal sutures. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(849, 65, ''Fontanelles are soft sports where two  or more sutures meets. There are two:  i) anterior fontanelles or bregma, is diamond in shape, situated at the junction of the sagittal, coronal and frontal sutures. It closes at 18 months. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(850, 65, ''ii)Posterior fontanelle (Lambda) is triangular in shape located at the junction of the sagittal and lambdoidel sutures. It closes earlier, at 6 months. 1mark'', ''0, 0.5, 1'', NULL),
(851, 65, ''Importance of the fetal skull ? takes part during labor 1/2Mark'', ''0,0.25,0.5'', NULL),
(852, 64, ''Student introduces self and task required   1/2marks'', ''0,0.25,0.5'', NULL),
(853, 64, ''Picks the model of the pelvis and fetus and places on the right occipito - posterior position 1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(854, 64, ''Lie  longitudinal, presentation  cephalic, position  ROPP  attitude deflexed, engaging diameter  occipito posterior 11.5cm,  1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(855, 64, ''Engagement and descent the fetal head enters the pelvis in an oblique diameter instead of the transverse  1/2marks'', ''0,0.25,0.5'', NULL),
(856, 64, ''Flexion the fetus flexes so as to navigate the birth canal with the smallest diameter 1/2marks'', ''0,0.25,0.5'', NULL),
(857, 64, ''Internal rotation With good flexion and uterine contractions, descent, the right occiput touches the pelvis floor muscles rotates 1/8th or 135 ? 155 degree forward to reach the symphysis pubis. (OA position)  1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(858, 64, ''If this long rotation fails, it results to persistent occipito posterior and baby is birth face to pubes 1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(859, 64, ''Crowning / extension if long rotation occurs to AO position, the head extends the pubic arch Crowning takes place 1 mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(860, 64, ''If POPP, the root of the nose engages under the symphysis pubis and the head flexes rather than extends to be delivered  1 mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(861, 64, ''Delivery of the head - External rotation/ restitution ? the head rotates back 45 degrees to align with the shoulders. 1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(862, 64, ''Delivery of the shoulder/ body or expulsion The shoulders enters and touches the pelvic floor , rotates forward, the anterior shoulders passes under the symphysis pubis 1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(863, 64, ''While the posterior shoulder is delivered and the body.1mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
