(982, 80, ''13. Gently insert the tube along the floor of the selected nostril, directing backward and downward. 1? mark'', ''0.5,0.75,1.5'', NULL),
(983, 80, ''14. When the tube reaches the oropharynx, instruct the patient to swallow as the tube advances. 1 mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(984, 80, ''15. Observe patient?s response; stop immediately if coughing, choking, or cyanosis occurs (may indicate tracheal entry). Withdraw tube slightly and reattempt if safe. 1 mark'', ''0,0.5,1'', NULL),
(985, 80, ''16. Confirm placement: aspirate gastric contents and test with litmus paper (acidic pH) or inject air and auscultate over the epigastrium for gurgling sound. 1 ? mark'', ''0.5,0.75,1.5'', NULL),
