(1288, 101, ''1. PreparationVerify the medical order, perform hand hygiene, gather the correct oxygen delivery device, and confirm the patient\'s identity using two identifiers.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1289, 101, ''2. AssessmentAssess the patient\'s vital signs, respiratory status, oxygen saturation levels, and patency of the nares or airway.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1290, 101, ''3. ExplanationExplain the procedure to the patient, outline the safety precautions regarding oxygen use, and obtain verbal consent.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1291, 101, ''4. Equipment CheckAttach the flowmeter to the oxygen source, connect the delivery tubing, and turn on the flow to ensure the system functions without leaks.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1292, 101, ''5. Flow AdjustmentAdjust the flowmeter to the exact prescribed liters per minute or percentage and ensure the humidifier bottle bubbles if it is being utilized.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1293, 101, ''6. ApplicationFit the oxygen device comfortably onto the patient\'s face or nose, adjusting the straps to ensure a secure but gentle seal.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1294, 101, ''7. Skin CarePad the tubing behind the ears and over bony prominences to prevent skin breakdown and friction injuries.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1295, 101, ''8. Safety CheckPost an oxygen safety sign in the room and verify that all ignition sources, friction toys, and smoking materials are removed'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1296, 101, ''9. Re-evaluationMonitor the patient\'s respiratory response, comfort level, and oxygen saturation via pulse oximetry within \\(15\\) to \\(30\\) minutes of initiation.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
(1297, 101, ''10. Post-CarePerform hand hygiene, dispose of waste materials appropriately, and document the flow rate, delivery device, and patient tolerance in the charts.'', ''0,0.5,1'', ''2026-06-29 09:58:04''),
